The code statements that lead to the bug are:
list_move_tail(&task->cg_list, &cset->mg_tasks);
Reason:
The list_move_tail moves the task from cset->tasks to cset->mg_tasks before advancing active iterators. As a result, when css_task_iter_skip() is later called (in css_set_move_task), the iterator advances relative to mg_tasks instead of the original tasks list, causing other tasks on cset->tasks and mg_tasks to be skipped.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
css_set_skip_task_iters(cset, task);
list_move_tail(&task->cg_list, &cset->mg_tasks);
Reason:
The addition of css_set_skip_task_iters before moving the task ensures that all active iterators pointing to this task are advanced to the next task on cset->tasks while the task is still on the correct list. This prevents the race where iterators would advance based on the wrong list after the move.

